  <notes>Running head "INDEX" with a small ornament after it; the ornament is not transcribed. No page number is printed. Uncertain readings marked [?]: "gelaus" (column 2, line 15, letter 'l' or 'o' unclear), "Licius" (column 2, "à gemellis"), and the Latin spelling of "gelaus", which may be "gelous". Several entries in the first column were written with a space or ligature that is hard to separate (e.g. "gammarus Andreas Petrus", "gasnerus", "gestius"); these are copied as they appear. Column 3 "gigas Casparus" is printed with a space ("Caspar us") and copied here as Casparus. Fine ligatures and superscript marks on "Sylvester" and "Gregorius" are read as printed. Some Latin forms (e.g. "Syluester"/"Sylvester", "Ducmistanus") are uncertain at this scan resolution.</notes>
